$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
oxazolines 5 Exemplified for the synthesis of 5{1,1,1}: Passerini adduct
3{1,1,1} (53 mg, 0.13 mmol, 1 eq) was dissolved in dry CH2Cl2 (3 ml) in a
8 ml MW vial (CEM), polymerbound triphenylphosphine (PL-TPP, 172 mg, 2
eq, loading = 1.52 mmol/g) bought from Polymer Labs was added and the
suspension was heated at 100°C by means of microwaves for 25 minutes (P =
150 W). After filtering the resin, the solution was concentrated under
reduced pressure. expected compound as a white yellowish solid that
needed no purification.
(4S)-N,4-dibenzyl-2-phenyl-4,5-dihydrooxazole-5-carboxamide 5{1,1,1}
(4S)-4-benzyl-N-tert-butyl-2-(pyridin-2-yl)-4,5-dihydrooxazole-5-carboxamide
5{1,2,2} White foam (41 mg, 100%). R f= 0.24 (silica gel, PE/EtOAc 2:8)
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3), mixture of diastereoisomers, δ = 8.71 (m, 2H),
8.12 (m, 2H), 7.81 (tt, J = 7.8, 1.8 Hz, 2H), 7.39 - 7.50 (m, 2H), 7.15 -
7.39 (m, 10H), 6.44 (s, 1H), 6.18 (s, 1H), 5.11 (d, J = 10.2 Hz, 1H),
4.78 - 4.90 (m, 1H), 4.73 (dd, J = 12.7, 6.3 Hz, 1H), 4.62 (d, J = 6.7
Hz, 1H), 3.32 (dd, J = 13.7, 3.3 Hz, 1H), 3.05 - 3.21 (m, 2H), 2.56 (dd,
J = 13.6, 11.6 Hz, 1H), 1.41 (s, 9H), 1.31 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3), mixture of diastereoisomers, δ = 169.3, 167.1, 161.2, 161.0,
149.8, 149.7, 146.4, 146.2, 138.7, 136.9, 136.8, 130.0, 129.6, 128.5,
128.4, 126.8, 126.5, 126.1, 126.0, 124.7, 124.3, 81.6, 81.3, 73.4, 70.3,
51.8, 51.4, 41.8, 37.3, 28.8, 28.7. GC-MS (E.I): r.t 9.94 mins m/z 337
[M] + (0.1), 237 (11), 147 (100), 57 (12) r.t 10.15 mins m/z 337 [M] +
(3), 207 (22), 194 (11), 148 (10), 147 (100), 132 (15), 115 (10), 105
(17), 91 (18), 78 (21), 57 (29), 41 (13) HRMS found: [MH+] 338.1866 ( -
0.8 ppm), C20H24N3O2 requires 338.1869.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, solid-supported reagent, Staudinger-aza-Wittig
reaction, 150W power, PL-TPP resin used (1.52 mmol/g loading, 2 eq.)
