$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 14 was promptly carried on in the next transformation. A
suspension of aldehyde 14 (160 mg, 0.40 mmol), polymerstyrene-supported
Ph3P (420 mg, 1.3 mmol) and freshly distilled THF (6.5 mL) was heated at
reflux for 9 h. The suspension was filtered and washed with THF and
concentrated to afford 15 as a colorless oil of excellent purity. Further
purification could be accomplished by flash column chromatography (SiO2,
10:1 EtOAc-MeOH) to afford 15. Methyl
(2S)-6-((2R,3R)-3-methyl-4,4-dihydro-2H-pyrrole-2-carboxamido)-2-(2,2,2-trifluoroacetamido)hexanoate
(15), yield (150 mg, 0.40 mmol, quantitative). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CD3CN) δ
(ppm): 8.02 (dd, 1H J = 5.1 Hz); 7.60 (s, 1H); 6.79 (br t, 1H, J = 5.1
Hz); 4.35 (ddd, 1H, J = 8.7, 7.5, 5.1 Hz); 3.94 (dq, 1H, J = 7.2, 2.4
Hz); 3.69 (s, 3H); 3.29- 3.10 (m, 2H); 2.79 (dddd, 1H, J = 17.4, 8.4,
2.1, 1.5 Hz); 2.33-2.19 (m, 2H); 2.21-2.12 (m, 1H); 1.89-1.74 (m, 2H);
1.55-1.40 (m, 2H); 1.39-1.29 (m, 2H); 1.17 (d, 3H, J = 6.6 Hz). 13C NMR
(75 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 173.4, 171.7, 170.2, 157.6 (q, J = 149.7 Hz),
117.0 (q, J = 114.2 Hz), 82.0, 53.6, 52.6, 45.7, 38.3, 35.4, 30.3, 29.3,
23.0, 19.9. HRESI-MS (TOF ES+) C15H27NO6 [M+H]+ calc. mass 366.1557,
measured 366.1553.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
