$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-4-(4-methylbenzyl)-5-oxo-2-phenyl-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6c, (184 mg, 99%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. (184 mg, 99%),
colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt), mp 160-161 °C; 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3)
δ 7.91 (dd, J = 1.5 Hz, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.69-7.67 (m, 2H, HAr),
7.44-7.28 (m, 5H, HAr), 7.22-7.16 (m, 3H, HAr), 6.97 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H,
HAr), 5.20 (s, 1H), 5.09 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 5.01 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H),
4.39 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 3.15-3.06 (m, 1H), 2.19 (s, 3H), 1.38-0.86 (m,
8H), 0.50-0.34 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.2 (Cq), 164.7 (Cq),
164.5 (Cq), 146.1 (Cq), 138.4 (Cq), 137.8 (Cq), 133.4 (Cq), 132.0 (CHAr),
130.9 (CHAr), 130.5 (CHAr), 129.9 (CHAr), 128.9 (CHAr), 128.6 (CHAr),
127.5 (CHAr), 127.0 (CHAr), 126.1 (CHAr), 125.8 (Cq), 59.0 (CH),
52.3(CH2), 47.9 (CH), 32.2 (CH2), 32.0 (CH2), 25.1 (CH2), 24.5 (CH2),
24.3 (CH2), 21.0 (CH3); IR (KBr) ν̃ 3324 (NH), 3057 (CHAr), 2927, 2850,
1679 (C=O), 1630 (C=O), 1527, 1456; EIMS m/z 465 (M+, 13), 340 (82), 277
(48), 235 (86), 179 (38), 105 (100), 77 (44); HRMS (EI) calcd for
C30H31N3O2: 465.2416; found 465.2418; Anal. Calcd for C30H31N3O2: C,
77.39; H, 6.71; N, 9.03. Found: C, 77.27; H, 6.62; N, 8.95.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Benzodiazepine β-Turn Mimetics by an Ugi
4CC/Staudinger/Aza-Wittig Sequence. Solving the Conformational Behavior
of the Ugi 4CC Adducts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
