$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-2-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)-4-(4-methylbenzyl)-5-oxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]-diazepine-3-carboxamide
6h, (207 mg, 99%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 99-100 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.90 (dd, J= 1.4 Hz, J= 7.9 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.48 (d,
J = 2.0 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.43-7.38 (m, 1H, HAr), 7.28 (d, J= 7.6 Hz, 1H,
HAr), 7.22-7.12 (m, 4H), 6.99 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H, HAr), 6.75 (d, J = 8.4
Hz, 1H, HAr), 5.20 (s, 1H), 5.13 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 5.05 (d, J =
8.4Hz, 1H), 4.35 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 3.86 (s, 6H), 3.15-3.06 (m, 1H),
2.21 (s, 3H), 1.37-0.86 (m, 8H), 0.51-0.35 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz,
CDCl3) δ 167.2 (Cq), 164.4 (Cq), 163.4 (Cq), 151.7(Cq), 149.0 (Cq), 146.3
(Cq), 138.2 (Cq), 133.2 (CHAr), 131.8 (CHAr), 130.5 (CHAr), 130.4 (CHAr),
129.7 (CHAr), 128.8 (CHAr), 126.8 (CHAr), 125.7 (Cq), 125.6 (CHAr), 120.9
(CHAr), 110.1 (CHAr), 109.9 (CHAr), 58.3 (CH), 55.8 (CH3), 55.8 (CH3),
52.1 (CH2), 47.7 (CH), 32.0 (CH2), 31.9 (CH2), 25.0 (CH2), 24.4 (CH2),
24.2 (CH2), 20.8 (CH3), IR (KBr) ν̃ 3338 (NH), 3060 (CHAr), 2918, 2853,
1683 (C=O), 1653 (C=O), 1613, 1576, 1501; EIMS m/z 526 (M+, 31); 400
(100); 395 (79); 105 (83); HRMS (EI) calcd for C32H35N3O4: 525.2628;
found 525.2632; Anal. Calcd for C32H35N3O4: C, 73.12; H, 6.71; N, 7.99.
Found: C, 73.19; H, 6.62; N, 8.09.
