$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-4-(4-fluorobenzyl)-2-(4-methoxyphenyl)-5-oxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6t, (196 mg, 99%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 160-161 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.91 (dd, J = 1.6 Hz, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H, HAr),
7.61-7.57 (m, 2H, HAr), 7.43-7.40 (m, 1H, HAr), 7.28-7.17 (m, 4H, HAr),
6.84-6.78 (m, 4H, HAr), 5.13 (s, 1H), 5.01 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 4.84 (d,
J = 14.4 Hz, 1H), 4.71 (d, J = 14.4 Hz, 1H), 3.79 (s, 3H), 3.22-3.10 (m,
1H), 1.38-0.78 (m, 8H), 0.54-0.41 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ
167.5 (Cq), 164.4 (Cq), 163.5 (Cq), 162.6 (d, 1J= 247.5 Hz, Cq), 162.2
(Cq), 146.2 (Cq), 132.2 (d, 4J= 3.1 Hz, Cq), 132.1 (CHAr), 130.7 (CHAr),
130.6 (CHAr), 129.3 (CHAr), 127.1 (CHAr), 126.0 (CHAr), 125.9 (Cq), 115.7
(d, 2J = 21.5 Hz, CHAr), 114.0 (CHAr), 58.9 (CH), 55.5 (CH3), 52.1 (CH2),
48.1 (CH), 32.3 (CH2), 32.2 (CH2), 25.1 (CH2), 24.5 (CH2), 24.5 (CH2); IR
(KBr) ν̃ 3325 (NH), 3062 (CHAr), 2932, 2851, 1678 (C=O), 1624 (C=O),
1570, 1510; EIMS m/z 499 (M+, 7), 374 (100), 265 (64), 109 (71); HRMS
(EI) calcd for C30H30N3O3F: 499.2271; found 499.2281; Anal. Calcd for
C30H30N3O3F: C, 72.13; H, 6.05; N, 8.41. Found: C, 72.21; H, 6.11; N,
8.36.
