$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Sodium Diaminodiphenylphosphonium Diazaylides 7'b, 7'd, 7'g; Typical
Procedure Into a three necked round-bottomed flask,
chlorodiphenylphosphine Ph2PCl (1.8 mL, 10 mmol) in anhyd THF (60 mL) was
introduced under N2, and Na (0.46 g, 20 mmol) was then added at 25 °C.
The mixture turns first yellow and then orange after 18 h in refluxing
THF. After cooling to 20 °C and elimination of excess Na by filtration,
the solution was introduced under N2, dropwise, to a solution of freshly
prepared acyl azide (20 mmol) in anhyd acetone (25 mL).6 N2 evolution can
be measured by H2O displacement. After 48 h at 20 °C, the yellow and
turbid solution was filtrated. The filtrate was evaporated to dryness to
give a solid corresponding to the crude diylide 7'. After
recrystallization, 7'b (EtOH) and 7'd (CH2Cl2) were both obtained in 40%
yield (4 mmol) (Tables 1 and 2). Compound 7'g was not stable enough to be
isolated but it was probably detected in situ by 31P NMR (Table 1) as the
lone phosphorus product of the reaction. 7'g, yield 99%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of stabilized diaminophosphonium diazaylides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
