$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-2-(4-methoxyphenyl)-4-(4-methylbenzyl)-5-oxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6e, (195 mg, 99%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 159-160 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.87 (dd, J= 1.5 Hz, J= 7.9 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.68-7.65
(m, 2H, HAr), 7.41-7.37 (m, 1H, HAr), 7.27-7.14 (m, 4H, HAr), 6.98 (d, J
= 10.9 Hz, 2H, HAr), 6.83-6.80 (m, 2H, HAr), 5.18 (s, 1H), 5.10 (d, J =
14.2 Hz, 1H), 5.01(d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 4.39 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 3.78
(s, 3H), 3.16-3.06 (m, 1H), 2.20 (s, 3H), 1.37-0.86 (m, 8H), 0.50-0.35
(m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.3 (Cq), 164.5 (Cq), 163.5 (Cq),
161.9 (Cq), 146.4 (Cq), 138.2 (Cq), 133.3 (CHAr), 131.8 (CHAr), 130.5
(CHAr), 130.3 (CHAr), 129.8 (CHAr), 129.3 (CHAr), 128.9 (CHAr), 126.9
(CHAr), 125.8 (Cq), 125.6 (CHAr), 113.8 (CHAr), 58.5 (CH), 55.3 (CH3),
52.2 (CH2), 47.8(CH), 32.1 (CH2), 31.9 (CH2), 25.1 (CH2), 24.4 (CH2),
24.3 (CH2), 20.9 (CH3); IR (KBr) ν̃ 3341 (NH), 3014 (CHAr), 2932, 2850,
2223, 1684 (C=O), 1624 (C=O), 1515, 1259; EIMS m/z 495 (M+, 32), 371
(26), 370 (100), 369 (30), 265 (88), 105 (71); HRMS (EI) calcd for
C31H33N3O3: 495.2522; found 495.2519; Anal. Calcd for C31H33N3O3: C,
75.13; H, 6.71; N, 8.48. Found: C, 75.02; H, 6.82; N, 8.33.
