$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the preparation of oxazolines 5 Exemplified for the
synthesis of 5{1,1,1}: Passerini adduct 3{1,1,1} (53 mg, 0.13 mmol, 1 eq)
was dissolved in dry CH2Cl2 (3 ml) in a 8 ml MW vial (CEM), polymerbound
triphenylphosphine (PL-TPP, 172 mg, 2 eq, loading = 1.52 mmol/g) bought
from Polymer Labs was added and the suspension was heated at 100°C by
means of microwaves for 25 minutes (P = 150 W). After filtering the
resin, the solution was concentrated under reduced pressure. expected
compound as a white yellowish solid that needed no purification.
(4S)-N,4-dibenzyl-2-phenyl-4,5-dihydrooxazole-5-carboxamide 5{1,1,1}
White yellowish foam (48 mg, 99%) R f= 0.46 (silica gel, PE/EtOAc 6:4) 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3), mixture of diastereoisomers, δ = 7.88 - 7.97(m,
2H), 7.16 - 7.55 (m, 28H), 6.67 (b, t, 1H), 6.48 (b, t, 1H), 5.18 (d, J =
10.2 Hz, 1H), 4.72 (d, J = 5.3 Hz, 1H), 4.29 - 4.92 (m, 6H), 3.25 (dd, J
= 13.7, 3.4 Hz, 1H), 3.05 - 3.20 (m, 2H), 2.59 (dd, J = 13.5, 10.7 Hz,
1H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3), mixture of diastereoisomers, δ = 170.43,
168.23, 161.90, 161.55, 138.58, 137.71, 136.93, 131.98, 130.08, 129.80,
128.96, 128.90, 128.64, 128.61, 128.55, 128.53, 128.38, 128.30, 128.03,
127.90, 127.78,127.73, 127.06, 126.82, 126.50, 81.01, 80.82, 72.90,
70.45, 43.28, 43.13, 42.00, 37.51. GC-MS (E.I): r.t. 13.31 mins; m/z 370
[M] + (1), 263 (8), 147 (11), 146 (100), 91 (57), 77 ( 10) r.t. 13.58
mins; m/z 370 [M] + (3), 206 (19), 147 (11), 146 (100), 91 (64), 77 (11)
HRMS found: [MH+] 371.1755 ( - 1.3 ppm), C24H23N2O2 requires 371.1760.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, solid-supported reagent, Staudinger-aza-Wittig
reaction, 150W power, PL-TPP resin used (1.52 mmol/g loading, 2 eq.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
