$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To prove whether compound 3{1,1,1} could be transformed into
β-benzoylamino-α-hydroxyamide 4 according to the PADAM protocol, it was
reacted with triphenylphosphine, known to reduce azides to amines via
phosphazene formation and subsequent hydrolysis. The reaction proceeded
smoothly in dichloromethane and water but, instead of 4 furnished
oxazoline 5{1,1,1} according to a Staudinger-Aza-Wittig (SAW) reaction
(Scheme 2). (4S)-N,4-dibenzyl-2-phenyl-4,5-dihydrooxazole-5-carboxamide
5{1,1,1}
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger-aza-Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
