$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-4-(4-fluorobenzyl)-5-oxo-2-phenyl-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6r, (186 mg, 99%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 160-161 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.92 (td, J = 1.4 Hz, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.61
(d, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H, HAr), 7.45-7.18 (m, 8H, HAr), 6.77 (dt, J = 1.5 Hz, J
= 8.5 Hz, 2H, HAr), 5.17 (s, 1H), 5.09 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 4.77 (s, 2H),
3.22-3.15 (m, 1H), 1.40-0.84 (m, 8H), 0.56-0.41 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz,
CDCl3) δ 167.6 (Cq), 164.8 (Cq), 164.6 (Cq), 162.8 (d, 1J = 247.7 Hz,
Cq), 146.3 (Cq), 137.9 (Cq), 132.5 (d, 4J = 3.2 Hz, Cq), 132.4 (CHAr),
131.3 (CHAr), 130.9 (CHAr), 130.9 (CHAr), 128.9 (CHAr), 127.7(CHAr),
127.4 (CHAr), 126.6 (CHAr), 126.1 (CHAr), 116.1 (CHAr), 162.8 (d, 2J =
247.7 Hz, CHAr), 59.7 (CH), 52.4 (CH2), 48.4 (CH), 32.5 (CH2), 32.5
(CH2), 25.4 (CH2), 24.8 (CH2), 24.7 (CH2); IR (KBr) ν̃ 3315 (NH), 3068
(CHAr), 2929, 2853, 1674 (C=O), 1636 (C=O), 1507; EIMS m/z 469 (M+, 12),
344 (100), 277 (32), 235 (50), 109 (71); HRMS (EI) calcd for C29H28N3O2F:
469.2166; found 469.2154; Anal. Calcd for C29H28N3O2F: C, 74.18; H, 6.01;
N, 8.95. Found: C, 74.12; H, 5.92; N, 8.86.
