$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Complex [3]. A solution of [2a] (330 mg, 0.82 mmol) and
triphenylphosphine (250 mg, 0.95 mmol) in dichloromethane (10 mL) was
stirred for 3 h at ambient temperature. The solvent was removed in vacuo,
and the residue was washed with diethyl ether (3 × 10 mL). Yield: 509 mg
(0.80 mmol, 98%) of a red solid. Complex [3], Yield: 509 mg (0.80 mmol,
98%) 1H NMR (400.1 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.58 (m, 6H, Arphosphine-H), 7.46 (m,
9H, Arphosphine-H), 5.46 (d, 2H, 3J = 6.0 Hz; Arcymene-H), 5.27 (d, 2H,
3J = 6.0 Hz, Arcymene-H), 3.86 (t, 2H, 3J = 6.6 Hz, CH2NC), 3.43 (dt, 2H,
3J = 6.6 Hz, 3J H,P = 15.2 Hz, CH2N=PPh3), 2.78 (sept, 1H, 3J = 6.9 Hz,
CH(CH3)2), 2.15 (s, 3H, Ar-CH3), 1.15 (d, 6H, 3J = 6.9 Hz, CH(CH3)2).
13C{1H} NMR (100.6 MHz, CDCl3): δ 137.9 (CN), 132.3 (d, JC,P = 9.2 Hz,
o-Cphosphine), 131.9 (d, JC,P = 2.3 Hz, p-Cphosphine), 128.8 (d, JC,P =
11.6 Hz; m-Cphosphine), 107.0, 106.6 (Arcymene-C-iPr and Arcymene-C-Me),
87.4, 87.2 (Arcymene-CH), 49.0 (d, 2JC,P = 23.0 Hz, CH2N=PPh3), 45.1 (d,
3JC,P = 2.3 Hz, CH2CH2N=PPh3), 31.0 (CH(CH3)2), 22.4 (CH(CH3)2), 18.7
(Ar-CH3). 13C{1H} NMR (162.0 MHz, CDCl3): δ 15.1 (br). IR (KBr, cm-1): ν˜
2204 (s, CN). MS (MALDI) m/z: 637 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety (. Aliphatic azides are high energy density materials. Vigorous
heating of 2-azidoethylamine did cause an explosive decomposition.
Organic azides should not be heated to temperatures higher than 100 oC.),
Staudinger reaction
