$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Si-G2(CHO)8 To a solution of dendron Si-Gj(PIII)4 (500 mg,
0.25 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (15 mL) was added dropwise a solution of azide 1
(368 mg, 1.05 mmol) in CH2Cl2(15 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at
room temperature for five hours and then evaporated to dryness. The crude
material was washed with 3 x 20 mL of ether to afford Si-G2(CHO)8 White
powder, yield 98% . 31P{1H} NMR (CDCl3) δ 13.7 (d, JP2P'2 = 30.1 Hz,
P'2), 19.2 (d, JPOPO = 33.9 Hz, P'0), 50.0 (d, JP2P2 = 30.1 Hz, P2), 51.7
(d, JPOPO = 33.9 Hz, P0), 60.9 (s, P'). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 0.73 (t, JHH =
8.1 Hz, 2H, CH2-Si), 1.10 (t, JHH = 7.0 Hz, 9H, CHs-CHz-O-Si), 1.86 (m,
2H, CH2-CH2-Si), 3.07 (m, 2H, P'0-CH2), 3.35 (d, JHPI = 11.0 Hz, 6H,
CH3-N-P]), 3.84 (q, JHH = 7.0 Hz, 6H, CH3- CHs-O-Si), 7.21-7.88 (m, 108H,
CH=N, Harom), 9.88 (s, 8H, CHO). 13C{1H) NMR (CDCl3) δ 11.5 (d, JCPO =
15.7 Hz, P'0-CH2-CH2-CH2), 15.7 (br s, P'0-CH2-CH2), 18.3 (s,
Si-O-CH2-CH3), 29.0 (d, JCPO = 65.0 Hz, P'0-CH2), 32.9 (d, JCPI = 13.6
Hz, CH2-N-P,), 58.4 (s, Si-O-CH2-CH3), 121.6 (d, JCPO = 4.2 Hz, CO2),
121.8 (d, JCPi = 5.2 Hz, C,2), 122.0 (d, JCP2 = 5.8 Hz, C22), 125.0 (dd,
JCP2 = 105 Hz, JCP2 = 6.0 Hz, Cj4), 127.7 (d, JCP2 = 112.1 HZ, C2'),
128.1 (s, C03), 128.7 (d, JCPO = 11.1 Hz, C0m), 128.8 (d, 2JCP2 = 12.7
Hz, C2m), 129.0 (d, JCPO = 117.5 Hz, Co1), 131.2 (s, C23), 131.4 (d, JCP,
= 10.2 Hz, C0°), 131.7 (s, C04), 132.3 (s, C0P), 132.6 (d, JCPO = 10.1
Hz,C2°), 132.7 (s, C2P)132.9 (s, C24), 134.6 (d, 1JCV2 = 12.8 Hz, Cj3),
140.5 (d, 3JCPI = 14.4 Hz, CH=N-N-Pi), 153.4 (d, JCPI = 9.1 Hz, Co1),
153,9 (br s, C1), 156.7 (d, JCP2 = 8.2 Hz, C21), 191.0 (s, CHO). IR
(KBr): 1702 cm-1 (VCHo). Anal. Calcd for C165H143N9O25Pi2S7Si (3276.2):
C, 60.49; H, 4.39; N, 3.84. Found: C, 60.57; H, 4.48; N, 3.76.
