$DATUM (2R,3S)-2-tert-Butyldimethylsiloxymethyl-3-vinyl-N,5-didehydropyrrolidine
(10a): To a solution of aldehyde 9 (7.6 g, 27 mmol) in THF (150 mL) was
added triphenylphosphine (8.5 g, 32 mmol) at r. t. in 6 small portions
over a period of 2 h. After stirring for an additional 12 h, the solvent
was evaporated. The residue was purified by flash column chromatography
(hexane/EtOAc, 1:1, ninhydrin detection on warmed TLC plates: intense
brown color) to give 10a as a oil. Pale yellow oil, yield 6.3 g, 98%.
[α]D20 - 27.4° (c = 2.1, CHCl3). 1H NMR (270 MHz): δ = 0.02 (s, 3 H),
0.04 (s, 3 H), 0.84, (s, 9 H), 2.28 (m, 1H), 2.70-2.84 (m, 2H), 3.80 (mc,
3H), 4.92 (dd, J2 = 10 Hz, J2 = 2 Hz, 1 H), 5.00 (dd, J2= 17.5 Hz, J2= 2
Hz, 1H), 5.76 (ddd, J2 = 17.5 Hz, J2= 10 Hz, J3= 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.52 (s,
1H). 13C NMR (68 MHz): δ = -5.44, -5.36, 18.26, 25.86, 41.60, 43.63,
64.40, 80.03, 114.27, 140.77, 166.24. IR (film, KBr): v = 3080 (w), 2955
(s), 2929 (s), 2897 (m), 2857 (s), 1640 (m), 1625 (m), 1472 (s), 1463
(m), 1432 (w), 1388 (w), 1361 (w), 1256 (s), 1193 (w), 1121 (s, br.),
1005 (m), 992 (m), 911 (m), 837 (vs), 776 (s), 670 cm-1 (m). MS (80 eV,
EI, 40°C): m/z (%) = 239 (0.1), 224 (2.3), 182 (100), 141 (1.7), 116
(1.8), 101 (1.6), 89 (3.7), 75 (6.0), 73 (10.5), 67 (3.5), 59 (5.2).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
