$DATUM (4R)-4-[(1S)-3-Benzoyloxy-(1-vinyl)propyl]-2-methyl-2-oxazoline (14): To
a solution of 13 (2.5 g, 7.9 mmol) in THF (10 mL) was added
triphenylphosphine (2.5 g, 9.5 mmol) at r. t. in 3 small portions over a
period of 1 h. After stirring at this temperature for additional 12 h,
the solvent was evaporated. The residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc, 1:1) to give 14 as a oil. Colorless oil,
yield 2.1 g, 97%. [α]D20 + 8.0° (c = 0.9, CHCl3). 1H NMR (250 MHz): δ =
1.64-1.78 (m, 1H), 1.94 (s, 3H), 2.16-2.32 (m, 2H), 3.88-4.04 (m, 2H),
4.18 (t, J=8Hz, 1 H), 4.20-4.40 (m, 2H), 5.08 (dd, J1 = 17.5 Hz, J2 = 2
Hz, 1II), 5.12 (dd, J1 = 10 Hz, J2 = 2 Hz, 1 H), 5.44 (ddd, J1 = 17.5 Hz,
J2 = 10 Hz, J3 = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.34-7.44 (m, 2H), 7.48-7.56 (m, 1H), 7.98
(dd, J1 = 10 Hz, J2 = 1.5 Hz, 2 H). 13C NMR (63 MHz): δ = 13.79, 30.07,
46.77, 62.96, 69.55, 70.60, 117.2, 128.23, 129.44, 130.29, 132.74,
137.34, 165.16, 166.39. IR (film, KBr): v = 3072 (w), 2972 (m), 2899 (m),
1718 (vs), 1676 (vs), 1602 (m), 1584 (w), 1452 (s), 1387 (s), 1315 (s),
1275 (s, br.), 1230 (m), 1176 (m), 1115 (s), 1071 (s), 1026 (s), 984 (s),
921 (m), 713 (vs), 688 (m), 675 cm-1 (w). MS (EI, 80 eV, 40°C): m/z (%) =
273 (1.2), 203 (1.9), 190 (3.4), 172 (1.7), 168 (5.4), 152 (3.5), 138
(1.8), 125 (20.7), 105 (70.3), 94 (5.1), 84 (95.0), 77 (71.0), 68 (100),
