$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure: to a solution of diphenylphosphine proline phenyl
ester 3b (103 mg, 0.274 mmol) in 3:1 mixture of DMF/pH 7.4 phosphate
buffer (2 mL) was added a solution of benzyl azide (38 mg, 0.28 mmol) in
the same solvent (1 mL) at room temperature. The reaction was monitored
by TLC and it was completed within 30 min at room temperature. The
reaction mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate (2 × 10 mL). The
combined organic layers were washed with water and brine then dried over
MgSO4 and concentrated. Purification by flash column chromatography with
3% MeOH in DCM gave the desired product 7. Yield 106 mg, 96 %. mp 43-46
°C; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.18 (t, J = 5.9 Hz, 1H), 7.75 (m, 4H),
7.62 - 7.18 (m, 11H), 4.51 - 4.30 (m, 2H), 4.07 (ddd, J = 8.1, 5.8, 2.2
Hz, 1H), 3.29 - 3.05 (m, 2H), 2.52 - 2.32 (m, 1H), 2.17 - 1.97 (m, 1H),
1.95 - 1.84 (m, 2H); 31P NMR (122 MHz, CDCl3) δ 28.44; 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 172.94, 138.67, 132.53, 132.48, 132.44, 132.39, 132.36, 132.26,
132.23, 129.13, 129.07, 128.97, 128.90, 128.82, 128.04, 127.49, 62.60,
62.57, 47.95, 47.90, 43.84, 31.29, 31.21, 25.36, 25.27; IR (thin film)
3260.4, 3060.2, 2941.7, 2872.2, 1653.5, 1511.5, 1437.9, 1167.1, 1102.8,
1062.0, 726.9, 694.2 cm-1; MS (ESI) m/z calcd for C24H26N2O2P [M+H]+
405.2, found 405.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on solvent, phosphate buffered solution
used, Staudinger ligation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A proline-based phosphine template for Staudinger ligation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Park, Chung-Min; Niu, Wei; Liu, Chunrong; Biggs, Tyler D.; Guo, Jiantao;
Xian, Ming
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(17), 4694-4697

