$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Si-G0(CHO)2. To a solution of (EtO)3Si-(CH2)3PPh2 (390 mg,
1.00 mmol) kept at 0 °C in CH2Cl2 (20 mL) was added dropwise a solution
of azide 1 (350 mg, 1.00 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (20 mL). The reaction mixture
was allowed to reach room temperature in 1 h and was then evaporated to
dryness. The foamy crude material was washed with 20 mL of pentane/ether
(2/1) to afford Si-G0(CHO)2. Colorless thick oil, yield 96%. 31P{1H} NMR
(CD3COCD3): δ 20.1 (d, 2JP0P'0 = 33.0 Hz, P0'), 50.5 (d, 2JP0P'0 = 33.0
Hz, P0). 1H NMR (CD3COCD3): δ 0.87 (t, 3JHH= 8.2 Hz, 2H, CH2-Si), 1.22
(t, 3JHH= 7.0 Hz, 9H, CH3-CH2-O-Si), 1.86 (m, 2H, CH2-CH2-Si), 3.08 (td,
3JHH= 8.2 Hz, 2JHP'0) 11.0 Hz, 2H, P0'-CH2), 3.86 (q, 3JHH= 7.0 Hz, 6H,
CH3-CH2-O-Si), 7.52-8.04 (m, 18H, Harom), 10.11 (s, 2H, CHO). 13C{1H} NMR
(CD3COCD3): 11.8 (d, 2JCP'0 = 15.0 Hz, P0'-CH2-CH2-CH2), 15.9 (d, 3JCP'0
= 3.0 Hz, P0'- CH2-CH2), 18.0 (s, Si-O-CH2-CH3), 29.2 (d, 1JCP'0 = 63.4
Hz, P0'-CH2), 58.2 (s, Si-O-CH2-CH3), 122.2 (d, 3JCP0 = 5.7 Hz, C02),
129.1 (d, 2JCP'0 = 13.7 Hz, C0 m), 129.5 (dd, 1JCP'0 = 102.9 Hz, 3JCP0 =
8.5 Hz, C0i), 131.1 (s, C03), 131.6 (d, 3JCP'0 = 11.5 Hz, C0o), 132.7 (br
s, C0 p), 133.3 (s, C0 4), 157.2 (d, 2JCP0 = 9.7 Hz, C0 1), 191.0 (s,
CHO). IR (KBr): 1702 cm-1 (ν 'CHO). Anal. Calcd for C35H41NO7P2SSi
(709.81): C, 59.22; H, 5.82; N, 1.97. Found: C, 59.09; H, 5.71; N, 2.04.
