$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-2-(4-fluorophenyl)-4-(4-methoxybenzyl)-5-oxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6l, (190 mg, 96%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 199-200 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.89 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.64-6.94 (m, 9H,
HAr), 6.64 (d, J= 8.6 Hz, 2H, HAr), 5.14 (s, 1H), 5.10 (d, J = 8.4 Hz,
1H), 4.84 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 4.60 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 3.64 (s, 3H),
3.18-3.04 (m, 1H), 1.37-0.86 (m, 8H), 0.58-0.34 ( m, 2H); 13C NMR
(100MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.2 (Cq), 164.4 (Cq), 164.3 (d, 1J = 252.4 Hz, Cq),
163.5 (Cq), 159.6 (Cq), 146.0 (Cq), 134.1 (d, 4J = 2.8 Hz, Cq), 132.1
(CHAr), 130.5 (CHAr), 130.2 (CHAr), 128.2 (CHAr), 127.0 (CHAr), 126.2
(CHAr), 125.7 (Cq), 115.5 (d,2 J = 21.9 Hz, CHAr), 114.4 (CHAr), 58.9
(CH), 55.1 (CH3), 52.0 (CH2), 48.0 (CH), 32.2 (CH2), 32.1 (CH2), 25.1
(CH2), 24.5 (CH2), 24.3 (CH2); IR (KBr) ν̃ 3308 (NH), 3063 (CHAr), 2932,
2856, 1674 (C=O), 1609 (C=N), 1521, 1451, 1222; EIMS m/z 499 (M+, 8), 374
(26), 278 (49), 277 (100), 253 (27), 121 (57); HRMS (EI) calcd for
C30H30N3O3F: 499.2271; found 499.2263; Anal. Calcd for C30H30N3O3F: C,
72.13; H, 6.05; N, 8.41. Found: C, 72.24; H, 6.11; N, 8.34.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Benzodiazepine β-Turn Mimetics by an Ugi
