$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis
3-[o-N-(Triphenylphosphoranylidene)phenyl]-4-(p-tolylsulfoxy)-5-phenylisoxazole
(11a): To a solution of
3-(o-azidophenyl)-4-(p-tolyl-sulfoxy)-5-phenylisoxazole (10a) (0.2000 g,
0.50 mmol, 1 equiv) in anhyd toluene (10 mL) was added at r.t., under an
atmosphere of dry nitrogen, a solution of triphenylphosphine (0.1311 g,
0.50 mmol, 1 equiv) in anhyd toluene (5 mL). The reaction mixture was
stirred for a total of 5 h whilst being monitored by TLC. After
completion of the reaction, the solvent was removed in vacuo and the
crude product was purified by flash silica column chromatography (eluent:
petroleum ether-EtOAc, 2:1) to give 3-[o-N-(triphenylphosphoranylidene)
phenyl]-4-(p-tolylsulfoxy)-5-phenylisoxazole. Compound 11b, yield 95%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The first aza-Wittig reaction involving a non-cumulated sulfoxy group
