$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-4-(4-methylbenzyl)-5-oxo-2-(4-methylphenyl)-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6d, (182 mg, 95%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 190-191 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.96 ( d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.65 (d, J = 8.0
Hz, 2H, HAr), 7.48-7.17 (m, 7H, HAr), 7.04 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H, HAr), 5.25
(s, 1H), 5.17 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 5.07 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 4.41 (d, J
= 14.2 Hz, 1H), 3.20-3.13 (m, 1H), 2.38 (s, 3H), 2.25 (s, 3H), 1.42-0.97
(m, 8H), 0.54-0.40 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.2 (Cq), 164.4
(Cq), 164.3 (Cq), 146.2 (Cq), 141.4 (Cq), 138.2 (Cq), 135.0 (Cq), 133.3
(Cq), 131.8 (CHAr), 130.4 (CHAr), 129.8 (CHAr), 129.2(CHAr), 128.8
(CHAr), 127.5 (CHAr), 126.9 (CHAr), 125.8 (CHAr), 125.8 (Cq), 58.6 (CH),
52.2 (CH2), 47.7 (CH), 32.1 (CH2), 31.9 (CH2), 25.1 (CH2), 24.4 (CH2),
24.2 (CH2), 21.3(CH3), 20.9 (CH3); IR (KBr) ν̃ 3335 (NH), 3019 (CHAr),
2916, 2861, 1679 (C=O), 1630 (C=O), 1516, 1451; EIMS m/z 479 (M+, 25),
354 (100), 277 (53), 249 (74), 105 (82); HRMS (EI) calcd for C31H33N3O2:
479.2573; found 479.2564; Anal. Calcd for C30H31N3O2: C, 77.63; H, 6.94;
N, 8.76. Found: C, 77.72; H, 6.81; N, 8.84.
