$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Triphenyliminophosphorane 5 3-Azidobenzofuran (4, 1 mmol) in
dry Et2O (3 mL) was slowly added to a solution of Ph3P (1 mmol) in dry
Et2O (3 mL) at 0 °C under a stream of nitrogen. The mixture was stirred
at 0 °C for 3 h and then at r.t. for an additional 1 h. Removal of the
solvent in vacuo afforded the title iminophosphorane. Yellow thick oil,
yield 95%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.23-7.70 (m, 16 H), 7.20 (t, J =
10.5 Hz, 2 H), 7.03 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1 H), 6.94 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H). 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 132.78, 132.71, 132.59, 132.51, 131.99, 131.75,
128.77, 128.67, 128.53, 128.44, 123.57, 121.18, 120.05, 119.84, 110.88,
110.67.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A new entry to benzo[4,5]furo[3,2-b]pyridines via
N-(benzofuran-3-yl)iminophosphorane
