$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-Methyl-5-phenyl-3,7,8,8a-tetrahydropyrido[4,3-d]pyrimidin-2(1H)-one
(6b). A solution of pyrimidine 5b (0.507 g, 1.78 mmol) and PPh3 (0.529 g,
2.02 mmol) in dry MeCN (40 ml) was refluxed for 7 h under stirring, and
then the solvent was removed in vacuum. The residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel 60 (17 g) eluting with CHCl3-MeOH
(from 100:0 to 20:1). Yield 0.403 g (95%), slightly yellow crystals. mp
197.0-197.5°C (decomp., MeCN). IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3188 (s), 3127 (s),
3086 (s), 3060 (s) (ν NH), 1717 (vs) (amide I), 1645 (s) (ν C═C), 1584
(m) (ν CC Ar), 1557 (s) (ν C═N), 1491 (m) (ν CC Ar), 705 (s) (δ CH Ar).
1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 8.53 (1H, br. s, 3-NH); 7.05 (1H, s,
1-NH); 7.48-7.34 (5H, m, H Ph); 4.14 (1H, ddq, 3J = 3J = 5.8, 5J = 1.4,
8a-CH); 3.82-3.73 (1H, m) and 3.37-3.28 (1H, m, 7-CH2); 1.81-1.61 (2H, m,
8-CH2); 1.30 (3H, d, 5J = 1.4, 4-CH3). 13C NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 165.7
(C-5); 154.0 (C-2); 141.4 (C-i Ph); 136.3 (C-4); 128.9 (C-4 Ph); 128.2
(C-3,5 Ph); 127.5 (C-2,6 Ph); 103.1 (C-4a); 47.6 (C-8a); 47.3 (C-7); 31.6
(C-8); 17.8 (CH3). Found, %: C 69.49; H 6.33; N 17.41. C14H15N3O
Calculated, %: C 69.69; H 6.27; N 17.41.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
