$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-4-(4-chlorobenzyl)-2-(4-methoxyphenyl)-5-oxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6o, (196 mg, 95%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 155-156 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, acetone-d6,) δ 7.87 (ddd, J= 0.5 Hz, J= 1.6 Hz, J= 7.9 Hz,
1H, HAr), 7.72-7.47 (m, 7H, HAr), 7.28-7.23 (m, 2H, HAr), 7.08-7.04 (m,
1H, HAr), 6.87-6.83 (m, 1H, HAr), 6.71 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 5.60 (s, 1H),
5.40 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.42 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.87 (s, 3H),
3.30-3.23 (m, 1H), 1.58-0.74 (m, 10H); 13C NMR (100MHz, acetone-d6) δ
168.7 (Cq), 166.5 (Cq), 166.1 (Cq), 163.6 (Cq), 148.3 (Cq), 138.1 (Cq),
135.9 (Cq), 134.5 (Cq), 133.5 (CHAr), 133.4 (CHAr), 132.9 (CHAr), 132.1
(CHAr), 132.0 (CHAr), 131.4 (CHAr), 130.3 (CHAr), 130.1 (CHAr), 130.0
(CHAr), 128.5 (Cq), 128.4 (CHAr), 126.8 (CHAr), 115.1 (CHAr), 61.2 (CH),
56.6 (CH3), 53.5 (CH2), 50.0 (CH), 33.7 (CH2), 33.6 (CH2), 26.9 (CH2),
26.6 (CH2), 26.5 (CH2); IR (KBr) ν̃ 3302 (NH), 3046 (CHAr), 2921, 2856,
1679 (C=O), 1641(C=O), 1511; EIMS m/z 515 (M+, 27), 392 (36), 391 (33),
390 (100), 389 (22), 266 (16), 265 (85), 239 (21), 238 (30), 237 (18),
209 (22); HRMS (EI) calcd for C30H30N3O3Cl: 515.1976; found 515.1973;
Anal. Calcd for C30H30N3O3Cl: C, 69.83; H, 5.86; N, 8.14. Found: C,
69.91; H, 5.77; N, 8.19.
