$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction of Azide derivatives with TPPc in Table 2 Azide derivatives
9a-9g (1 equiv) and 2 (1.1 equiv) were dissolved in THF-H2O (5 mL, 9:1,
v/v). A mixture was stirred at room temperature for 2 h and evaporated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel to
give primary amino derivatives 10a-10g. 0.1M concentration of azide
derivatives in the reaction solvent was used in this study. 9a, 10a, 10b:
Commercially available Benzyl amine 10a 1H-NMR (CD3OD) δ 7.44 (5H, s),
4.11 (2H, s)
