$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the One-Pot Conversion
of an Azido to an Amido Group. To a solution of 1.0 mmol of α-azidoester
and 944 mg (2.5 mmol) of p-nitrophenyl palmitate in 30 mL of THF/H2O 9:1
was added 314 mg (1.2 mmol) of Ph3P. The reaction mixture was stirred at
room temperature under nitrogen for 48 h (96 h for a phytoceramide
precursor). After the solvents were removed in vacuo (2-PrOH was used to
remove the residual H2O), the light yellow residue was dissolved in 100
mL of Et2O and washed with 1% aqueous Na2CO3 solution (4 X 20 mL) to
remove the 4-nitrophenol byproduct. The organic phase was dried (Na2SO4)
and concentrated. The residue was purified by column chromatography
(elution with hexane/EtOAc 5:1). Ethyl
(2R,3S,4R)-2-palmitoylamido-3-hydroxy-4-(methoxymethyloxy) octadecanoate
[(-)-11]. Ethyl
(2R,3S,4S)-2-palmitoylamido-3-hydroxy-4-(methoxymethyloxy)octadecanoate
[(-)-11']. yield 94%. mp 58.8-59.4 °C; [α]25D -8.24° (c 1.93, CHCl3); IR
3510, 1742, 1652 cm-1; 1H NMR δ 0.86 (t, 6H, J = 7.0 Hz), 1.20-1.42 (m,
49H), 1.60 (m, 3H), 1.74 (m, 1H), 2.22 (t, 2H, J = 7.6 Hz), 2.65 (br s,
1H), 3.39 (s, 3H), 3.54 (m, 1H), 3.70 (dd, 1H, J = 6.0, 3.8 Hz), 4.20 (m,
2H), 4.63 (d, 1H, J = 6.8 Hz), 4.70 (dd, 1H, J = 8.5, 3.7 Hz), 4.72 (d,
1H, J = 6.9 Hz), 6.47 (d, 1H, J = 8.4 Hz); 13C NMR δ 14.11, 22.68, 25.20,
25.55, 29.23, 29.35, 29.48, 29.57, 29.61, 29.65, 29.68, 31.15, 31.91,
36.54, 54.22, 55.94, 61.52, 74.37, 82.40, 97.86, 170.35, 174.16; HR-MS
(FAB, MH+) calcd for m/z C38H76NO6 642.5672, found 642.5654.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
