$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Staudinger Ligation of
substrates 9a-9i. To a solution of diphenylphosphine proline phenyl ester
3b in 3:1 DMF-phosphate buffer (pH 7.4) was added 1.1 equiv. of the
corresponding azido amino acid or peptide in the same solvent system at
room temperature. The final concentration of 3b was 0.1~ 0.08 M. The
reaction was completed usually within 30 min at room temperature. Work-up
procedure was the same as mentioned before. Purification by flash column
chromatography with 3~ 10 % MeOH in DCM gave the desired products.
Compound 9d, colorless oil, yield 94%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.47 (t,
J = 6.0 Hz, 1H), 7.69 - 7.46 (m, 3H), 7.39 (m, 6H), 7.32 - 7.09 (m, 10H),
6.96 - 6.80 (m, 1H), 4.90 (dt, J = 9.8, 6.0 Hz, 1H), 4.59 - 4.32 (m, 2H),
3.95 (q, J = 5.9 Hz, 1H), 3.37 (dd, J = 13.8, 6.3 Hz, 1H), 3.19 - 2.97
(m, 2H), 2.91 (m, 1H), 2.14 - 2.01 (m, 2H), 1.75 (m, 1H), 1.62 - 1.39 (m,
1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 172.50, 171.16, 157.02, 138.94, 136.92,
132.81, 132.78, 132.65, 132.62, 132.35, 132.22, 131.88, 131.75, 131.39,
130.27, 129.72, 129.67, 129.28, 129.11, 128.94, 128.89, 128.79, 128.63,
128.49, 128.36, 127.09, 119.92, 115.73, 62.02, 61.98, 53.48, 50.01,
49.97, 43.66, 38.19, 32.12, 32.04, 25.21, 25.12; IR (thin film) 3395.2,
3268.6, 3060.2, 3027.5, 2937.6, 1652.4, 1503.3, 1433.8, 1176.4, 1119.2,
910.8, 726.9, 698.3 cm-1; MS (ESI) m/z calcd for C28H32N4O4P [M+H]+
519.2, found 519.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM phosphate buffered solution used, Staudinger ligation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
