$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the One-Pot Conversion of an Azido to an Amido
Group. To a solution of 1.0 mmol of α-azidoester and 944 mg (2.5 mmol) of
p-nitrophenyl palmitate in 30 mL of THF/H2O 9:1 was added 314 mg (1.2
mmol) of Ph3P. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature under
nitrogen for 48 h (96 h for a phytoceramide precursor). After the
solvents were removed in vacuo (2-PrOH was used to remove the residual
H2O), the light yellow residue was dissolved in 100 mL of Et2O and washed
with 1% aqueous Na2CO3 solution (4 X 20 mL) to remove the 4-nitrophenol
byproduct. The organic phase was dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated. The
residue was purified by column chromatography (elution with hexane/EtOAc
5:1). Ethyl (2R,3S,4R)-2-palmitoylamido-3-hydroxy-4-(methoxymethyloxy)
octadecanoate [(-)-11]. yield 94%. mp 58.6-59.2 °C; [α]25D -32.95° (c
1.39, CHCl3); IR 3537, 1738, 1654 cm-1; 1H NMR δ 0.84 (t, 6H, J = 7.0
Hz), 1.15-1.42 (m, 51H), 1.62 (m, 4H), 2.24 (t, 2H, J = 7.6 Hz), 3.34 (s,
3H), 3.48 (m, 1H), 3.82 (br s, 1H), 4.01 (dd, 1H, J = 7.1, 2.7 Hz), 4.16
(m, 2H), 4.51 (dd, 2H, J = 12.3, 6.5 Hz), 4.67 (dd, 1H, J = 6.7, 2.8 Hz),
6.67 (d, 1H, J = 6.6 Hz); 13C NMR δ 13.96, 14.06, 22.64, 24.35, 25.52,
29.20, 29.28, 29.31, 29.43, 29.56, 29.61, 29.65, 29.83, 30.64, 31.88,
36.36, 55.83, 56.10, 61.61, 73.70, 80.18, 97.13, 170.24, 174.59; HR-MS
(FAB, MH+) calcd for m/z C38H76NO6 642.5672, found 642.5636.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Stereocontrolled, Efficient Synthetic Route to Bioactive Sphingolipids:
Synthesis of Phytosphingosine and Phytoceramides from Unsaturated Ester
Precursors via Cyclic Sulfate Intermediates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM He, Linli; Byun, Hoe-Sup; Bittman, Robert
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2000), 65(22), 7618-7626

