$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
oxazolines 5 Exemplified for the synthesis of 5{1,1,1}: Passerini adduct
3{1,1,1} (53 mg, 0.13 mmol, 1 eq) was dissolved in dry CH2Cl2 (3 ml) in a
8 ml MW vial (CEM), polymerbound triphenylphosphine (PL-TPP, 172 mg, 2
eq, loading = 1.52 mmol/g) bought from Polymer Labs was added and the
suspension was heated at 100°C by means of microwaves for 25 minutes (P =
150 W). After filtering the resin, the solution was concentrated under
reduced pressure. expected compound as a white yellowish solid that
needed no purification.
(4S)-N,4-dibenzyl-2-phenyl-4,5-dihydrooxazole-5-carboxamide 5{1,1,1}
Benzyl (5-(benzylcarbamoyl)-4,5-dihydrooxazol-2-yl)methylcarbamate
5{2,5,1} Thick yellow oil (133 mg, 93%) R f= 0.18 (silica gel, PE/EtOAc
1:9) 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 7.15 - 7.43 (m, 10H), 7.07 (b, s, 1H),
5.59 (b, s, 1H), 4.83 - 5.05 (m, 3H), 4.51 (dd, J = 14.8, 6.4 Hz, 1H),
4.34 (dd, J = 14.8, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 3.88 - 4.24 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3) δ = 170.4, 163.7, 156.8, 137.7, 136.1, 128.8, 128.6, 128.4, 128.1,
127.9, 127.7, 77.7, 67.3, 59.3, 43.2, 38.4. GC-MS: This method could not
be applied in this case. HRMS found: [MH+] 368.1614 (+ 1.0 ppm) ,
C20H22N3O4 requires 368.1610.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, solid-supported reagent, Staudinger-aza-Wittig
reaction, 150W power, PL-TPP resin used (1.52 mmol/g loading, 2 eq.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 5-Carboxamide-oxazolines with a
Passerini-Zhu/Staudinger-Aza-Wittig Two-Step Protocol
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
