$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method B: Compound 5 (0.50 mmol) and phosphine
derivative 2-4 (1.1 equiv) or triphenylphosphine (1.1 equiv) was
dissolved in THF-H2O (5 mL, 9:1, v/v). A mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 2 h and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
preparative thin layer chromatography eluted with hexane/EtOAc (50:50,
v/v). 6 and 7. 0.1M concentration of azide derivatives in the reaction
solvent was used in this study. Entry: 6b; compound: 6; yield: 93%.
Methyl-4-aminobenzoate 6 6 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.84 (2H, d, J = 8.4 Hz),
6.66 (2H, d, J = 8.4 Hz), 4.04 (2H, brs), 3.85 (3H, s).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM yield depends on reaction conditions (time)
