$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Enamines 3; Typical Procedure
Synthesis of 3-[(2,2-Diethoxyethyl)amino]-1-phenylbut-2-en-1-one (3x) To
benzoylacetone (0.200 g, 1.2 mmol) and 2-azido-1,1-diethoxyethane (2)
(0.236 g, 1.5 mmol) in THF (10 mL) was added Ph3P (0.656 g, 2.5 mmol) at
20 °C. The reaction mixture was heated and stirred for 8 h at reflux.
After cooling to 20 °C, the solvent was removed in vacuo and the residue
was purified by column chromatography (silica gel, n-hexane-EtOAc, 100:1
→ 1:1) to give 3x.
3-[(2,2-Diethoxyethyl)amino]-5,5-dimethylcyclohex-2-en-1-one (6b)
Starting with dimedone (5b) (0.421 g, 3.0 mmol),
2-azido-1,1-diethoxyethane (2a) (0.573 g, 3.6 mmol), and Ph3P (1.180 g,
4.5 mmol) in THF (15 mL), 6b was isolated after chromatography (silica
gel, n-hexane-EtOAc, 50:1 → EtOAc → acetone) as a light yellow oil (0.703
g, 92%). IR (neat): 3259 (m), 3069 (m), 2967 (s), 2935 (s), 2878 (s),
1738 (m), 1540 (s), 1452 (s), 1425 (m), 1410 (m), 1376 (s), 1271 (s),
1242 (s), 1131 (s), 1065 (s), 960 (w), 932 (w), 891 (w), 809 (m), 732
(m), 703 (w), 660 (w), 607 (m), 560 (m), 482 cm-1 (w). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300
MHz): δ = 1.07 (s, 6 H, 2 × CH3), 1.22 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 6 H, 2 × CH3),
2.17 (s, 2 H, CH2), 2.27 (s, 2 H, CH2), 3.23 (dd, J = 5.4, 5.4 Hz, 2 H,
NCH2), 3.50-3.60 (m, 2 H, OCH2), 3.65-3.75 (m, 2 H, OCH2), 4.67 (t, J =
5.4 Hz, 1 H, OCH), 5.12 (s, 1 H, CH=C), 5.89 (br s, 1 H, NH). 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ = 14.9 (2 × CH3), 27.8 (2 × CH3), 32.3 (C), 42.8
(CH2), 44.9 (NCH2), 49.9 (CH2), 62.2 (2 × OCH2), 94.6 (CH=C), 99.1 (OCH),
163.2 (N-C=CH), 196.2 (C=O). MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 255 (M+, 8), 210
(2), 181 (2), 164 (6), 151 (2), 138 (2), 122 (1), 103 (77), 84 (100), 75
(47). HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd for C14H25NO3 [M+]: 255.1829; found: 255.1824
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety, Staudinger-aza-Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 3-acylpyrroles, 3-(alkoxycarbonyl)pyrroles,
1,5,6,7-tetrahydro-4H-indol-4-ones and 3-benzoylpyridines based on
Staudinger-aza-Wittig reactions of 1,3-dicarbonyl compounds with 2- and
3-azido-1,1-dialkoxyalkanes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
