$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Enamines 3; Typical Procedure
Synthesis of 3-[(2,2-Diethoxyethyl)amino]-1-phenylbut-2-en-1-one (3x) To
benzoylacetone (0.200 g, 1.2 mmol) and 2-azido-1,1-diethoxyethane (2)
(0.236 g, 1.5 mmol) in THF (10 mL) was added Ph3P (0.656 g, 2.5 mmol) at
20 °C. The reaction mixture was heated and stirred for 8 h at reflux.
After cooling to 20 °C, the solvent was removed in vacuo and the residue
was purified by column chromatography (silica gel, n-hexane-EtOAc, 100:1
→ 1:1) to give 3x.
3-[(2,2-Diethoxyethyl)amino]-5-phenylcyclohex-2-en-1-one (6d) Starting
with 5-phenyl-1,3-cyclohexanedione (5d) (0.588 g, 3.0 mmol),
2-azido-1,1-diethoxyethane (2a) (0.573 g, 3.6 mmol) and Ph3P (1.180, 4.5
mmol) in THF (15 mL), 6d was isolated after chromatography (silica gel,
n-hexane-EtOAc, 50:1 → EtOAc) as a light brown solid (0.838 g, 92%). IR
(KBr): 3243 (s), 3065 (s), 2975 (m), 2934 (m), 2888 (m), 1545 (s), 1441
(s), 1374 (m), 1274 (s), 1239 (s), 1133 (s), 1069 (s), 757 (w), 701 cm-1
(w). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ = 1.23 (dt, J = 7.2, 1.4 Hz, 6 H, 2 ×
CH3), 2.44-2.75 (m, 4 H, 2 × CH2), 3.24 (dd, J = 5.1, 5.1 Hz, 2 H, NCH2),
3.29-3.41 (m, 1 H, CHPh), 3.50-3.61 (m, 2 H, OCH2), 3.66-3.76 (m, 2 H,
OCH2), 4.65 (t, J = 5.1 Hz, 1 H, OCH), 4.81 (br s, 1 H, NH), 5.22 (s, 1
H, CH = C), 7.23-7.27 (m, 3 H, 3 × CH of Ph), 7.31-7.34 (m, 2 H, 2 × CH
of Ph). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ = 15.0 (2 × CH3), 36.8 (CH2), 39.6
(CHPh), 43.3 (NCH2), 45.1 (CH2), 62.4 (2 × OCH2), 96.1 (CH=C), 99.2
(OCH), 126.4 (2 C), 126.6, 128.4 (2 C, CH of Ph), 142.9 (C of Ph), 163.6
(N-C=CH), 196.1 (C=O). MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 303 (M+, 8), 258 (3),
213 (7), 200 (4), 170 (5), 103 (100), 91 (46), 77 (32). HRMS (ESI): m/z
calcd for C18H25NO3 [M+]: 303.18344; found: 303.18338. UV/Vis (MeCN,):
λmax (log ε) = 280 nm (4.29).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety, Staudinger-aza-Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 3-acylpyrroles, 3-(alkoxycarbonyl)pyrroles,
1,5,6,7-tetrahydro-4H-indol-4-ones and 3-benzoylpyridines based on
Staudinger-aza-Wittig reactions of 1,3-dicarbonyl compounds with 2- and
3-azido-1,1-dialkoxyalkanes
